Package: virtuallte
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, kmod
Description: virtual 5G/LTE UE exposed as a USB CDC-MBIM modem
 VirtualLTE is a userspace UE (user equipment) that speaks the UERANSIM RLS
 protocol toward a gNB and presents itself to the host as a USB CDC-MBIM modem
 through the Linux USB raw-gadget interface. It implements 5G NAS registration,
 PDU sessions, a threaded user-plane data path, and SMS over IMS (MO and MT).
 .
 Each UE instance is driven by a configuration file under /etc/virtuallte/ and
 managed by the virtuallte@.service systemd template. For example,
 "virtuallte@ue1" reads /etc/virtuallte/ue1.conf.
